+## Sales
+
+- A sale line is one dish sold `qty` times (a whole number) on a till
+  ticket. It uses one recipe portion per dish; the ingredients are consumed
+  with ledger ref `sale:<ticket>` at `soldAt`, and the quantities used are
+  kept on the sale (`uses`). Sales are stored in `sales`.
+- A ticket is imported once: tickets already in `sales` are skipped. A
+  sales file is imported all or nothing.
+- Variance per item over days: theoretical use is the `uses` of sales sold
+  in those days; actual use is every `consume` movement in those days;
+  `difference` is actual minus theoretical.
+
